    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="0715" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/655: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-17T15:00:00+09:00">May 17, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 17—6:31 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>316. Our 314, May 17, 11 a.m.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d750-f1"/> We have now fully
                    registered our position. I am reluctantly of the opinion that further
                    representations along these lines by us at present would accomplish no
                    constructive results.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d750-f1" n="91" xml:id="d750-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; for memorandum of May 17 recording oral representations to the
                    Japanese Minister for Foreign Affairs, see <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_743"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol.
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 743</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
